meta {
  name: 54 Get Effective Accession Settings
  type: http
  seq: 54
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/settings/effective
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the effective Accession Module Settings (same shape as 34)", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("MasterData_TubeTypes");
    expect(d).to.have.property("MasterData_RejectionReasons");
    expect(d).to.have.property("MasterData_LogisticsTypes");
    expect(d).to.have.property("SampleBarcodeSettings_Preview");
    expect(d).to.have.property("Accession_MaximumTimeToAcceptSampleMinutes");
  });
}

docs {
  The active branch's Accession Module Settings **as they apply** — the read
  the operational screens use (In-House / Internal Referral / External
  Referral / Outsource worklists, Sample Search, Order Overview) for the Master
  Data lists (tube types, sample conditions, repeat / rejection reasons,
  discard methods, logistics types) and the acceptance rules.

  Login-only (no settings permission needed). The
  `accession:accession_settings__view_accession_settings` /
  `__update_accession_settings` permissions control who may open and change
  the Accession Settings page (`GET`/`PUT /accession/settings`, requests 34/35),
  never whether the saved settings take effect — so a user without them still
  gets the real saved values here, not the defaults.

  Same effective object as request 34: the branch's stored settings merged over
  the module defaults, plus the tenant-wide barcode counters/previews. Read-only.
  Tenant + branch come from the JWT / active profile. A caller with no active
  branch gets 404 (`BRANCH_NOT_FOUND`), like request 34.
}
